                <pb facs="0137" n="17" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg17"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.6363/1151: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-29T14:00:00-05:00">July 29, 1931—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:09 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>102. My 100, July 24, 11 a.m. President Olaya and Minister of Industries have
                    signed petroleum regulating decree. The decree, <pb facs="0138" n="18"
                        xml:id="pg18"/> however, has not yet been published in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Diario</hi>. It is highly satisfactory. Please inform
                    Mr. Rublee.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
